  HPLC.WU
I would like here to collect some notes on the curve fitting of RTIMEB.DA
 data on Dec. 22-26 1981.
   With the program HPLCWD.F4 (MATD28.F4) I succeeded to fit the data
using weights as 1/n**2 and all 27 parameters.  the values are:

  W   1.20147
  F   0.95230
  L   0.45511
  I  -0.01987
  Y   0.72021
  V   0.73891
  M   0.77829
  P   0.29465
  A  -0.00101
  N  -0.30359
  Q   0.20828
  G  -0.10718
  S   0.24268
  T   0.15203
  X  -0.50582
  D  -0.19820
  E  -0.03689
  C   0.60364
  R   0.35209
  H   0.66691
  K  -0.08121
TML  -3.84182
AEC   0.88877
 AC   0.51912
 NH   0.71199
 A*  25.99436
 C*  -8.78095
  I think, however that a weighting factor of 1/n might be better.
changed HPLCWD.F4 to this for the next series.
   Note that I have fitted these data without weights but kept
W,F,L,I,& Y fixed for the fitting.
